#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133642 :question/id #uuid "132af6fa-454c-596c-a057-dfe531792102" :question/math-academy-id "e-6283" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of $f(x,y,z) = \\dfrac{x}{yz}$ along the curve parametrized by $\\mathbf{r}(t) = t^2\\, \\mathbf{i} + t \\,\\mathbf{j} + 1 \\,\\mathbf{k}$ for $t \\in [0,\\sqrt 2].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $\\mathbf{r}(t) =t^2\\, \\mathbf{i} + t \\,\\mathbf{j} + 1 \\,\\mathbf{k},$ then along the curve we have $x = t^2,$ $y = t,$ and $z=1.$  \n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\,k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+1\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z) = \\dfrac{x}{yz},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{t\\cdot 1}=t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u= 4t^2+1,$ $\\textrm d u=8t\\,\\textrm d t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{1}{8}{u}^{1/2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[{9}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[27-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot 26 \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133644 :question/id #uuid "f07dd3d3-606f-520f-a95e-04303aa32f24" :question/math-academy-id "e-6307" :question/problem "Find an integral that is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle\\int\\limits_C xy^3 \\, \\textrm{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $\\mathbf r(t)= \\left \\langle \\cos t, \\sin t \\right\\rangle$ for $t \\in \\left(0, \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f5/f53d78debfec5f8c50e0f3a5947d2a36126e18c073d7b0cc4c59d506753059b3.png)\n\nThe path of integration is shown above. We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, we have $f(x,y) =  xy^3$. Along the path, we have $x=\\cos t$ and $y=\\sin t,$ and so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =f(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{3} \\\\  & ={sin}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C xy^3 \\, \\textrm{d}s = \\int^{\\pi/2}_{0} \\sin^3 t \\cos t \\, \\textrm{d}t .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133645 :question/id #uuid "8bf6a863-9b9f-5877-84bc-3e11d71261c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-6308" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle\\int\\limits_{C}xy\\,\\textrm{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $\\mathbf{r}(t) = 3t\\,\\mathbf{i}+4t\\,\\mathbf{j}\\,$ for $0\\leq t\\leq 1.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_a^b  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $\\mathbf{r}(t) = 3t\\,\\mathbf{i}+4t\\,\\mathbf{j},$ then along the curve we have $x=3t$ and $y=4t.$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)j \\\\  & =3\\,i+4\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y) =xy,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =3t\\cdot 4t \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}xy\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}12{t}^{2}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =60{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =60{[\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =20{[{t}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134276 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e006fbf-73db-5714-80d3-da70e1961752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324338} {:answer/id #uuid "4454bda2-b710-5b8e-962a-af8f72db9bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324524} {:answer/id #uuid "969d3d60-bae9-5b94-bb58-6e2e78279810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}-1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325255} {:answer/id #uuid "dc88ce8a-6d69-5cce-ae62-6e652a14c027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325896} {:answer/id #uuid "e1fc0716-e381-59ad-99c7-f5348e2706dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e006fbf-73db-5714-80d3-da70e1961752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324338} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa3112f0-f6c4-537c-b0c9-7b639ee76cae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "13f50e74-e351-581a-98f5-c8e27aa5380d" :question/math-academy-id "q-40253" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2}(x-y)$ and the curve $C$ is parametrized \n by $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+t,\\,{t}^{2}-t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,\\sqrt{2}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+t,\\,{t}^{2}-t⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2}+t,$ and $y={t}^{2}-t.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t)j \\\\  & =(2t+1)\\,i+(2t-1)\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t+1)^{2}+(2t-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+4t+1+4{t}^{2}-4t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2}(x-y)$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\sqrt{2}[({t}^{2}+t)-({t}^{2}-t)] \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}2\\sqrt{2}t\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134277 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c13ee6c3-92c9-5a3d-b1c3-cc0e6dc9c11d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{96}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131702} {:answer/id #uuid "dd83dc0f-ae75-597e-9bf5-97ca5882c46e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131703} {:answer/id #uuid "23b2b615-b99c-50e0-a324-227c7235fe42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{104}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131704} {:answer/id #uuid "442792c7-4dbd-5bc7-83a1-8c1fbcc8e6af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{62}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131705} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3b94ad-f1e1-5a06-b9fd-7ea4ca4724ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{54}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131706}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ae85dffa-91e2-5047-afe6-7098bbee9ba4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131701}] :question/id #uuid "b920de5e-825e-5dcf-9aac-175e4a51e8a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-40258" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x, y) = 3x$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $$\n\\displaystyle r(t) = ⟨\\frac{4t^{3/2}}{3}, \\frac{t^{2}}{2} - t⟩\n$$ for $t ∈ [0, 1]$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "867e1617-e755-5f5e-a7fd-c9f0fce495d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54(1 + π^{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132068} {:answer/id #uuid "f9a0a023-4af9-5c74-84ad-835ca54417c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54π^{2}(1 + 2π^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132069} {:answer/id #uuid "ff4c3273-3648-5e4d-a894-45f38532de5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27(1 + 2π^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132070} {:answer/id #uuid "1b35ab1c-0cdc-51c6-a919-098edbb8b942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18π^{2}(1 + 2π^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132071} {:answer/id #uuid "2640c3d9-c841-5fee-a9ae-5536944db3b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54(1 + π^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132072}] :answer-field/id #uuid "edacb75a-137f-5143-b6be-80a383127ae4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132067}] :question/id #uuid "38682a53-16b6-5629-9f8b-b56796ac3444" :question/math-academy-id "q-41160" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_(C)(x^{2} + y^{2})ds,\n$$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $r(t) = 3(\\cos t + t\\sin t)i + 3(\\sin t - t\\cos t)j$ for $0 \\le t \\le 2π$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134511 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07e37f47-83d1-5088-9b85-0e2e24287bf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342305} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac14869-5cac-504f-add3-8e9d269fda7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342328} {:answer/id #uuid "a0ae148b-fb50-5f08-a2c0-8a72efe39137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343656} {:answer/id #uuid "a2572c76-84e6-542d-8804-715f0e7d0f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343665} {:answer/id #uuid "eed4f8df-a5a6-55f1-8a77-0e82d4221bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eed4f8df-a5a6-55f1-8a77-0e82d4221bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344337} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f0f7cf8-f8e0-5481-a04a-8c128f9e6dec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a42a0c64-6afa-5778-a107-25576497d815" :question/math-academy-id "q-76186" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{12x}{y-1}$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(t+1)\\,j\\,$ for $t\\in [\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{6}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(t+1)\\,j$, then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2}$ and $y=t+1.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{12x}{y-1}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{12{t}^{2}}{(t+1)-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12{t}^{2}}{t} \\\\  & =12t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{6}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{6}}12t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=4{t}^{2}+1,$ $\\text{d}u=8t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{6}}12t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{9}^{25}\\frac{3}{2}{u}^{1/2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={u}^{3/2}{|}_{9}^{25} \\\\  & ={25}^{3/2}-{9}^{3/2} \\\\  & =125-27 \\\\  & =98\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4206dd2-7f0d-5a39-81ac-42f0f7afd440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}(\\sqrt{2} - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133111} {:answer/id #uuid "bef21a17-bc41-51cb-bd6f-ccfb84019bda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133112} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e019f4-70de-5a92-a4ca-84b324f58dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(2\\sqrt{2} + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133113} {:answer/id #uuid "1e9f6d66-d570-59cd-b849-c86b67cd5b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133114} {:answer/id #uuid "721bd124-318f-520e-bd5c-2af024eb5c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}(2\\sqrt{2} - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133115}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3dc97926-178c-5cd1-8a7d-3f12cff0ecfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133110}] :question/id #uuid "04dc89d7-54ea-5f6e-88f3-7fb468d7a9b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-76187" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_(C)4yz\\cos xds,\n$$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t) = ti + \\sin tj + k$ for $0 < t < \\frac{π}{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134513 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f149a5c8-374a-5613-9e94-f7a85f4e3578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2}(8t^{3} + t - 2)dt$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133117} {:answer/id #uuid "07f01a2c-6102-5f57-9a81-827ca9995533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2}(4t^{3} - 3)dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133118} {:answer/id #uuid "0e53f525-69b5-5819-9c6b-7b1f40a1280e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2}(t^{3} - t^{2} + 4t)dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133119} {:answer/id #uuid "0f8c7275-20d2-58af-b910-a3018cd7a77a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2}(8t^{3} - t^{2} + 4t - 4)dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133120} {:answer/id #uuid "4cb682b0-7b0d-59e5-8435-a35378e856c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2}(8t^{3} + t^{2} - 4)dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133121}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4ee84ab5-a5cf-5da3-83b7-b25c4dfcdc31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186133116}] :question/id #uuid "2f8d1c23-74d2-5539-9285-abeec9fd6ac3" :question/math-academy-id "q-76368" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_(C)(x^{3} - y)ds,\n$$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t) = 2ti + (2 - t)j$ for $-1 \\le t \\le 2$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284590 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "263de2e3-27ae-52e2-8582-4dfb39ba6ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}+1)\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282023} {:answer/id #uuid "75614e75-3308-50a7-a253-f1f9b76e3296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{t}^{2}}{\\sqrt{2t+1}}\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282694} {:answer/id #uuid "76433ca0-b7f8-577e-a495-c0ae272242e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282701} {:answer/id #uuid "89172764-a6f4-5672-8136-d35db577b74a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t(2t+1)\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282872} {:answer/id #uuid "8caffd9e-930e-5e4b-b97e-bcbc15c29c0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76433ca0-b7f8-577e-a495-c0ae272242e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282701} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee764035-aa19-5d16-9448-a4b9dd4171f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1bb4ae8a-0b75-5e62-bc9b-0900b739960b" :question/math-academy-id "q-167608" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\text{d}s,\n$$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j\\,$ for $0\\le t\\le 1?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=t$ and $y={t}^{2}.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i+2tj \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{4y+1}$, then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\left(\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1}\\right)\\cdot \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284591 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48320d50-11dc-5c25-b211-1a6293887c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282299} {:answer/id #uuid "667ecc69-8180-56b1-a381-85cc0e7c7286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282577} {:answer/id #uuid "7b621e50-9338-5847-b8c4-30f5e5589d2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282748} {:answer/id #uuid "90c1007a-4679-560a-84f7-593c87ce0e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282941} {:answer/id #uuid "9ac19e51-1f63-5f51-98b2-8211bafdd295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48320d50-11dc-5c25-b211-1a6293887c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282299} :answer-field/id #uuid "69141054-77da-5506-94da-51c42eb49c54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "72644873-b2ba-57a8-bd4c-d5dc5e8e5941" :question/math-academy-id "q-167609" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=x+y$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨t,\\,1+t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=⟨t,\\,1+t⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=t$ and $y=1+t.$    \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+t)j \\\\  & =\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x+y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =t+(1+t)=2t+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t+1)\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2t+1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{[{t}^{2}+t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(1+1-0) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284592 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c74ebde-4483-557d-bc7f-96d2eae35d76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281803} {:answer/id #uuid "3c1f1600-c667-5053-87bf-a32e6404cd47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14(2\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282216} {:answer/id #uuid "8298ffad-58f2-5c03-8c84-d9f00f0346bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7(2\\sqrt{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282818} {:answer/id #uuid "c84c1cb8-787a-5d55-a741-7cdf8092bf77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283442} {:answer/id #uuid "e3bd9128-7071-5f60-80ca-f9fcc77741a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{2}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c1f1600-c667-5053-87bf-a32e6404cd47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14(2\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282216} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c701af0-373b-5ef2-ba21-ba5e8d9c684f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c2dda2ab-f3d6-5a31-a33f-5b15f55a34c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-167612" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{3}+y$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)=3t\\,i+{t}^{3}\\,j\\,$ for $t\\in [0,1].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=3t\\,i+{t}^{3}\\,j$, then along the curve we have $x=3t$ and $y={t}^{3}.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,j \\\\  & =3\\,i+3{t}^{2}\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{(3{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{3}+y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(3t)^{3}+{t}^{3} \\\\  & =27{t}^{3}+{t}^{3} \\\\  & =28{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}28{t}^{3}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}84{t}^{3}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=1+{t}^{4},$ $\\text{d}u=4{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}84{t}^{3}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}21\\cdot {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =21\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =14({2}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =14(2\\sqrt{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10206875-a5c4-5022-9ee9-43b3a21b42b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281836} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd849f2-6a5c-5409-a292-f59a3dc7a36a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282215} {:answer/id #uuid "4544a980-713e-5e34-893c-6b08076a1997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282275} {:answer/id #uuid "7f63b4af-1a8d-5157-bbb0-dc8287c37b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282786} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a5f08d-e51f-5026-8bb2-63d5b7342f7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f63b4af-1a8d-5157-bbb0-dc8287c37b95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282786} :answer-field/id #uuid "b92feada-828f-5f43-8105-e8387a4f1f6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2907fc18-ef26-5825-bc1f-b4cb4bdbf7cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-167621" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}(2{x}^{2}-16)\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $r(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$  \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}-16$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-16 \\\\  & =16(2{cos}^{2}⁡t-1) \\\\  & =16\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(2{x}^{2}-16)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}16\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =64{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =64{[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t]}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =32[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0] \\\\  & =32(1-0) \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345213 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "372a5048-17c2-5076-9635-4ff4ad531da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{\\int }_{0}^{3}({t}^{2}+2t-1)\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342693} {:answer/id #uuid "60710012-7ccb-54d9-aac8-7c21a4db39de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343056} {:answer/id #uuid "7143c54a-f0e9-502c-b646-975daaf14a0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{\\int }_{0}^{3}t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343209} {:answer/id #uuid "77d755de-6003-5532-a85f-2d9e8cb137d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}({t}^{2}-2t)\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343274} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8c1d1a-5321-50f7-aff8-7b81e9c745ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}({t}^{2}+2t)\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60710012-7ccb-54d9-aac8-7c21a4db39de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343056} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d47b24e-5186-5a2c-bc62-0a4991b4b99e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e477990a-d15e-595b-a078-39c7382f9c05" :question/math-academy-id "q-76377" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $f(x,y,z)=2x-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}$ and the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,t-1,\\,t+1⟩$ for $t\\in [0,3]?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,t-1,\\,t+1⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2},$ $y=t-1,$ and $z=t+1.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+j+k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=2x-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2({t}^{2})-(t-1)^{2}-(t+1)^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-({t}^{2}-2t+1)-({t}^{2}+2t+1) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-{t}^{2}+2t-1-{t}^{2}-2t-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-2)\\cdot \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-2)\\cdot \\sqrt{2(2{t}^{2}+1)}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-2)\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2157cbec-dd3c-50c6-8f66-e922ba1f66ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342514} {:answer/id #uuid "46847ff5-553b-5f26-9805-09a27496f196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342819} {:answer/id #uuid "52b6665a-0ccb-5b28-87e4-9cb8ee2700ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi -1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342928} {:answer/id #uuid "a88c1662-aadb-5062-a115-55611ab6c159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343722} {:answer/id #uuid "bfef22ae-f97c-5172-89a1-1bc5619b881d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46847ff5-553b-5f26-9805-09a27496f196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342819} :answer-field/id #uuid "09fe84d2-3042-5159-a1de-85adb6692d1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344513}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5649582e-ddb6-5db4-a7c3-699a007eaafe" :question/math-academy-id "q-76433" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$  \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if $f(x,y)={y}^{2}$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & ={(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}=4{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}4{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\left(\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2}\\right)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{[t-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}{2}]}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =4[(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2})-0] \\\\  & =\\pi -2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345219 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d7aeab2-63a6-55b6-9670-af11f7878d7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342743} {:answer/id #uuid "55aaa22c-0a54-5244-a488-f06f0ea67eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342950} {:answer/id #uuid "7df5078f-cc9c-5640-bdbe-c73ad5edaf2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343323} {:answer/id #uuid "d44736e7-181c-5708-8fc6-091f82bf604a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344100} {:answer/id #uuid "ebc86749-0a58-547d-b292-dd0c15c33cf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55aaa22c-0a54-5244-a488-f06f0ea67eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342950} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddbabc5e-406f-59f6-a3fe-8b87b2e1d083" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a7a51cb6-cac0-57a7-bccc-fcb3f00d4af4" :question/math-academy-id "q-76434" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{y-x}$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨t,\\,t-4⟩$ for $t\\in [0,4].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=⟨t,\\,t-4⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=t$ and $y=t-4.$     \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-4)j \\\\  & =i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{y-x}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{t-(4-t)}=-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,\\cdot \\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}t\\,{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\cdot (4-0) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345220 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "330a0610-7510-562c-a947-1ed175f73e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342669} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec7f114-71dd-5707-a837-49ec4e0f58d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343037} {:answer/id #uuid "784dc8af-a9a4-53e0-8947-d481e7980aa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343277} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5af1a3-65b7-5d58-b8b9-b68cc63abf8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343333} {:answer/id #uuid "e3af6d11-71f3-548a-854f-ff88ce98cd06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "330a0610-7510-562c-a947-1ed175f73e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342669} :answer-field/id #uuid "b827e50e-d12a-5657-bed2-ba45d90ca8cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a6c30ef5-4b00-5501-a5b6-18892cf4af06" :question/math-academy-id "q-76447" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}({x}^{3}-2{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $C$ is the curve parametrized by $r(t)=4{t}^{2}\\,i+3{t}^{2}\\,j$ for $0\\le t\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=4{t}^{2}\\,i+3{t}^{2}\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=4{t}^{2}$ and $y=3{t}^{2}.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})j \\\\  & =8t\\,i+6t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(8t)^{2}+(6t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64{t}^{2}+36{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =10|t| \\\\  & =10t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t|=t$ since $t>0$ along the path of $C.$ \n\nNow, if $f(x,y)={x}^{3}-2{y}^{3}$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & ={(4{t}^{2})}^{3}-2{(3{t}^{2})}^{3} \\\\  & ={4}^{3}{t}^{6}-2\\cdot {3}^{3}{t}^{6} \\\\  & =64{t}^{6}-54{t}^{6} \\\\  & =10{t}^{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}({x}^{3}-{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10{t}^{6}\\cdot 10t\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =100{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{7}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =100\\cdot \\frac{{t}^{8}}{8}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =100[\\frac{{1}^{8}}{8}+\\frac{{0}^{8}}{8}] \\\\  & =100\\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =12.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345223 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec86e50-8126-5c8c-9c9e-7b518ae7992e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342364} {:answer/id #uuid "7c8f2e2d-51c7-5375-9e3c-dedb16da721e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343311} {:answer/id #uuid "a735d400-c4c3-527f-96ac-bc42ae20a5ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343710} {:answer/id #uuid "adb27abf-79df-56ff-bf2b-b4946023e074" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343766} {:answer/id #uuid "c49fb48e-7c9d-51a8-92b1-9e4b43f6a2e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c49fb48e-7c9d-51a8-92b1-9e4b43f6a2e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343969} :answer-field/id #uuid "c75af4f4-1064-571f-8598-a6fa76be3720" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5d73cf87-1a19-5cca-88b7-764818d04cb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-76479" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$  along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i-{t}^{2}\\,j$ for $0<t<\\sqrt{\\pi /2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i-{t}^{2}\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2}$ and $y=-{t}^{2}.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,j-2t\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(-2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}|t| \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t|=t$ because $t>0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}\\,t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u={t}^{2}$, $\\text{d}u=2t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{t}^{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}\\,t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345225 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a4b14bf-da94-5587-9476-c6c9f1763513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342466} {:answer/id #uuid "1dd66d9f-895b-589b-a593-4fcc58493314" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342486} {:answer/id #uuid "1ee36c09-cb9f-5764-9a87-cf5b7c3eff99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342494} {:answer/id #uuid "2b3d5513-4913-5c07-b97e-b502cd923def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342600} {:answer/id #uuid "5b5cec4d-eafc-5470-8930-282ed398fa90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ee36c09-cb9f-5764-9a87-cf5b7c3eff99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342494} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e475247-06f5-5122-b5e7-edfc19026889" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8ffd2389-f864-5810-9cd3-9a41b1f9dc53" :question/math-academy-id "q-76484" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{5},$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $r(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ and $y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$   \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =5|\\operatorname{cos}⁡t| \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ because $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\ge 0$ when $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{5}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{sin}^{2}⁡t}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{25{sin}^{2}⁡t}{5} \\\\  & =5{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}5{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =25{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =25{\\int }_{0}^{1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =25\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =25(\\frac{1}{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b563221-3548-560c-9fc8-b290090582fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342472} {:answer/id #uuid "34a3d682-f094-5b8e-9966-be8b9fc8ad8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342675} {:answer/id #uuid "618e4548-1271-521c-9a14-4e3337de95f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}-3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343065} {:answer/id #uuid "cd843b1d-6720-54f4-98b0-8e4c42afe883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344048} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f98bc6-232d-5249-b4a6-3f2a6e7f4860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{5}-3\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4f98bc6-232d-5249-b4a6-3f2a6e7f4860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{5}-3\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344249} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf920228-2dc2-55b3-a8f5-efbc9659d941" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344829}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "004b67de-a618-52fc-b8e0-1a45d41d2be5" :question/math-academy-id "q-76496" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}\\frac{y+z}{x}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $$\n\\displaystyle r(t)=t\\,i+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\,j+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\,k\n$$\nfor $1<t<\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $$\n\\displaystyle r(t)=t\\,i+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\,j+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\,k,\n$$ then along the curve we have $x=t,$ $y=\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2},$ and $z=\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,k \\\\  & =i+t\\,j+t\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+2{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=\\frac{y+z}{x}$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}}{t}=t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{y+z}{x}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{1+2{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=1+2{t}^{2}$, $\\text{d}u=4t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}t\\sqrt{1+2{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{3}^{5}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{3}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}({5}^{3/2}-{3}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{5}-3\\sqrt{3}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393618 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f72ef384-5e6e-52c5-839e-3beee185405e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{2}\\sqrt{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393620} {:answer/id #uuid "42147aee-d1b6-54a9-a34c-6883f2cfc5ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393621} {:answer/id #uuid "38308454-7a76-5601-988c-cc81a2d49d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{2}-t)\\sqrt{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393622} {:answer/id #uuid "9d940168-caf2-55dc-abc9-6478a8eb7fed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{2}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}-t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393623} {:answer/id #uuid "89f9a881-2016-5d9d-b0c2-417ca0dbf7d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{2}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42147aee-d1b6-54a9-a34c-6883f2cfc5ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393621} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc0d4305-f486-5b23-8a23-7975fef766e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9dd51c2a-c921-500f-b456-d9efa51cbc02" :question/math-academy-id "q-76356" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where $f(x,y,z)=x+y-z$ and the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+1,\\,{t}^{2}-1,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,2]?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+1,\\,{t}^{2}-1,\\,{t}^{2}⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x={t}^{2}+1,$ $y={t}^{2}-1,$ and $z={t}^{2}.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+1)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-1)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+2t\\,j+2t\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}|t| \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t|=t$ since $t>0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=x+y-z$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =({t}^{2}+1)+({t}^{2}-1)-{t}^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-{t}^{2} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}t\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393625 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa31ddbb-d2dc-5e24-b119-3e57906a0e43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393627} {:answer/id #uuid "6e191add-76d4-52b0-a4d0-b55782dad06f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393628} {:answer/id #uuid "e78b94bc-a9b3-5508-8e70-1864ef024d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393629} {:answer/id #uuid "0c7e2485-49a8-54d2-9942-acfa1e262b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393630} {:answer/id #uuid "1e167558-c450-5d8c-885f-dd7f2edd9925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e191add-76d4-52b0-a4d0-b55782dad06f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393628} :answer-field/id #uuid "80947165-9047-5b9a-b812-2946d21a42e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cfad2296-6fbf-598f-a4ed-63e51e9c1622" :question/math-academy-id "q-76379" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\,+t\\,k$ for $\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\,+t\\,k,$ then along the curve we have $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ and $z=t.$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}+{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\right)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, if $f(x,y,z)=z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =t((\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}) \\\\  & =t({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}z({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520663 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43ad5b43-aace-5d3d-a358-724cb263373e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2688}{5} - \\frac{784384 \\sqrt{2}}{945}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520675} {:answer/id #uuid "488a74d3-7dcc-59c5-a18f-dfc26f0e4a2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 - \\frac{128 \\sqrt{2}}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520676} {:answer/id #uuid "ba09aabf-f5f1-5b41-8fdb-b6dacd6f5500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520707} {:answer/id #uuid "dac02ed1-55d3-5134-9bb8-1308a80f0326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{8704 \\sqrt{2}}{105}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520720} {:answer/id #uuid "e19d4737-fdde-54f7-b02d-3480dff1be65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64 - \\frac{8704 \\sqrt{2}}{105}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e19d4737-fdde-54f7-b02d-3480dff1be65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64 - \\frac{8704 \\sqrt{2}}{105}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520723} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1997853-2be2-51a6-9186-222b0926a788" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520706}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "145cd2cc-e119-5363-8df0-50511cd77f67" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=- x - 3 y$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $$\n\\displaystyle r(t)=⟨\\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3},\\,2 t^{2} - 4 t⟩\n$$ for $t\\in [0,2].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $$\n\\displaystyle r(t)=⟨\\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3},\\,2 t^{2} - 4 t⟩,\n$$ then along the curve we have $x=\\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}$ and $y=2 t^{2} - 4 t.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t^{2} - 4 t)j \\\\ &=(8 \\sqrt{t})i+(4 t - 4)j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(8 \\sqrt{t})^2+(4 t - 4)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{64t+16(t-1)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{16(t^2+2t+1)} \\\\ &=4|t+1| \\\\ &=4 t + 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t+1|=t+1$ since $t\\geq0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=- x - 3 y$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(-1)\\left(\\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)+(-3)(2 t^{2} - 4 t) \\\\ &=- \\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} - 6 t^{2} + 12 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C - x - 3 y\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{2}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2}(- \\frac{16 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} - 6 t^{2} + 12 t)\\cdot (4 t + 4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2}- \\frac{64}{3}t^{3/2}(t+1)+(-48)(t^2/2-t)(t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2}- \\frac{64 t^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{3} - \\frac{64 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} - 24 t^{3} + 24 t^{2} + 48 t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[\\left(- \\frac{128 t^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{21}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{128 t^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{15}\\right)+(- 6 t^{4})+(8 t^{3})+(24 t^{2})\\right]_{0}^{2} \\\\ &=\\left(\\left(- \\frac{128 (2)^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{21}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{128 (2)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{15}\\right)+(- 6 (2)^{4})+(8 (2)^{3})+(24 (2)^{2})\\right)-\\left(\\left(- \\frac{128 (0)^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{21}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{128 (0)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{15}\\right)+(- 6 (0)^{4})+(8 (0)^{3})+(24 (0)^{2})\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(\\left(- \\frac{1024 \\sqrt{2}}{21}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{512 \\sqrt{2}}{15}\\right)+(-96)+(64)+(96)\\right)-\\left((0)+(0)+(0)+(0)+(0)\\right) \\\\ &=64 - \\frac{8704 \\sqrt{2}}{105}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "400cf204-a287-54da-8cf6-8f6c5520cca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520673} {:answer/id #uuid "a20dac01-182b-507b-bf2f-639fa423045a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "940" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520700} {:answer/id #uuid "aa3bf514-31bd-5be2-b51b-27b23cca2950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{212050}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520703} {:answer/id #uuid "adb18c45-c4c6-5d1a-bc95-d4057d6c1d2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1582}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520704} {:answer/id #uuid "d53c1a86-d5cc-5a33-a7f3-31c1f8e70e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5940" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d53c1a86-d5cc-5a33-a7f3-31c1f8e70e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5940" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520718} :answer-field/id #uuid "67baca2f-3def-5b74-8464-fcb9eed2a55b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2136d6d7-0ed7-55ff-b190-1b731f49a8bb" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=2 x^{2} + 2 y^{2} - 3$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩$ for $t\\in [1,3].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=- 5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ &=(5)(-\\sin t+\\sin t+t\\cos t)i+(5)(\\cos t-\\cos t+t\\sin t)j \\\\ &=(5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+(5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{25t^2(\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t)} \\\\ &=5|t| \\\\ &=5 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t|=t$ since $t\\geq0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=2 x^{2} + 2 y^{2} - 3$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(2)\\left((5 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(- 5 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 5 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2\\right)+(-3) \\\\ &=(50)\\left(\\cos^2t+2t\\sin t\\cos t+t^2\\sin^2t+\\sin^2t-2t\\sin t\\cos t+t^2\\cos^2t\\right)+(-3) \\\\ &=(50)(1+t^2)+(-3) \\\\ &=50 t^{2} + 47\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C 2 x^{2} + 2 y^{2} - 3\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{1}^{3}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{3}(50 t^{2} + 47)\\cdot (5 t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{3}250 t^{3} + 235 t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[\\left(\\frac{235 t^{2}}{2}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{125 t^{4}}{2}\\right)\\right]_{1}^{3} \\\\ &=\\left(\\left(\\frac{235 (3)^{2}}{2}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{125 (3)^{4}}{2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{235 (1)^{2}}{2}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{125 (1)^{4}}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(\\left(\\frac{2115}{2}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{10125}{2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{235}{2}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{125}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=5940.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520670 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4d59fc-515b-5f6a-9dc6-509c6e675345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520665} {:answer/id #uuid "48c82739-041c-56fa-8753-1bfa7fa0ee17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520677} {:answer/id #uuid "5e065b1b-4ec3-533f-9c2b-6e064e094ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520681} {:answer/id #uuid "797a833b-97df-53a4-a250-ba3c8eab7778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520692} {:answer/id #uuid "d047b09d-1678-5550-904c-27b96dd5e577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e065b1b-4ec3-533f-9c2b-6e064e094ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520681} :answer-field/id #uuid "dffa612e-a99a-5518-aa59-ddebaf8c26ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2cfdc280-62d5-528b-8c5c-9974a8b2cb2c" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=2 x + 2 y$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨- 2 t,\\,- 2 t - 2⟩$ for $t\\in [-2,0].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨- 2 t,\\,- 2 t - 2⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=- 2 t$ and $y=- 2 t - 2.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 2 t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 2 t - 2)j \\\\ &=(-2)i+(-2)j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(-2)^2+(-2)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{8} \\\\ &=2 \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=2 x + 2 y$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(2)\\left(- 2 t+(- 2 t - 2)\\right) \\\\ &=- 8 t - 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C 2 x + 2 y\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{-2}^{0}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-2}^{0}(- 8 t - 4)\\cdot (2 \\sqrt{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=(2 \\sqrt{2})\\int_{-2}^{0}- 8 t - 4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-2}^{0}- 16 \\sqrt{2} t - 8 \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=(4 \\sqrt{2})\\left[- 2 t^{2}+(- 2 t)\\right]_{-2}^{0} \\\\ &=\\left[(- 8 \\sqrt{2} t^{2})+(- 8 \\sqrt{2} t)\\right]_{-2}^{0} \\\\ &=\\left((- 8 \\sqrt{2} (0)^{2})+(- 8 \\sqrt{2} (0))\\right)-\\left((- 8 \\sqrt{2} (-2)^{2})+(- 8 \\sqrt{2} (-2))\\right) \\\\ &=\\left((0)+(0)\\right)-\\left((- 32 \\sqrt{2})+(16 \\sqrt{2})\\right) \\\\ &=16 \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520686 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03873494-83c0-5778-9053-50e3cd0a8960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520659} {:answer/id #uuid "067f6b16-2ef2-5fc3-a21a-839c972f0942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2} - \\frac{27 \\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520661} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2be384-eb81-581d-887c-e86a86517461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520680} {:answer/id #uuid "74ba6b0b-7f7b-585f-8489-1ebb8057a589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{81}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520689} {:answer/id #uuid "c6be7094-4eda-5791-84ae-661427999cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6be7094-4eda-5791-84ae-661427999cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520713} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b93d243-d980-5d5b-a615-915dffb75464" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520669}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6b0f1fc6-a816-51a9-b852-0409900ea7be" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=9 - 2 x^{2}$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩$ for $t\\in [- \\frac{\\pi}{2},- \\frac{\\pi}{4}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ &=(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})i+(- 3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(- 3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{9\\sin^2t+9\\cos^2t} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{9(\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t)} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{9} \\\\ &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=9 - 2 x^{2}$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(-1)\\left(2(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2-9\\right) \\\\ &=(-9)(2\\cos^2t-1) \\\\ &=- 9 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C 9 - 2 x^{2}\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}(- 9 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)})\\cdot (3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}- 27 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=-27\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\cos 2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=(-27)\\left[\\frac{1}{2}\\sin 2t\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\\\ &=\\left[\\left(- \\frac{27 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\\\ &=\\left(\\left(- \\frac{27 \\sin{\\left(2 \\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(- \\frac{27 \\sin{\\left(2 \\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(\\left(\\frac{27}{2}\\right)\\right)-\\left((0)\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26cafdf9-bb1b-5db6-9f2c-63c617017df2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520667} {:answer/id #uuid "3d86a63d-975f-514b-aa2d-6a9a2dda1a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520672} {:answer/id #uuid "649c7469-e587-53cb-ad3a-e1aa2a960ad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520682} {:answer/id #uuid "8b6f206b-ea3f-54ac-8df3-223331b388be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520696} {:answer/id #uuid "f6004e5c-0f89-546c-9a29-395a9815c45a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d86a63d-975f-514b-aa2d-6a9a2dda1a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520672} :answer-field/id #uuid "94de007f-b740-55aa-979f-480b58ced30a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6d171fb6-8597-5d32-b391-80e23689046f" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=- 2 x - 2 y$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨- t,\\,1 - t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,3].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨- t,\\,1 - t⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=- t$ and $y=1 - t.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1 - t)j \\\\ &=(-1)i+(-1)j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(-1)^2+(-1)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=- 2 x - 2 y$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(-2)\\left(- t+(1 - t)\\right) \\\\ &=4 t - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C - 2 x - 2 y\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{3}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{3}(4 t - 2)\\cdot (\\sqrt{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=(\\sqrt{2})\\int_{0}^{3}4 t - 2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{3}4 \\sqrt{2} t - 2 \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=(- 2 \\sqrt{2})\\left[- t^{2}+(t)\\right]_{0}^{3} \\\\ &=\\left[(2 \\sqrt{2} t^{2})+(- 2 \\sqrt{2} t)\\right]_{0}^{3} \\\\ &=\\left((2 \\sqrt{2} (3)^{2})+(- 2 \\sqrt{2} (3))\\right)-\\left((2 \\sqrt{2} (0)^{2})+(- 2 \\sqrt{2} (0))\\right) \\\\ &=\\left((18 \\sqrt{2})+(- 6 \\sqrt{2})\\right)-\\left((0)+(0)\\right) \\\\ &=12 \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520693 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48c9bce6-a245-551e-932e-0da2c01469dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{32 \\pi^{3}}{3} - 34 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520678} {:answer/id #uuid "67d2b09b-2ddd-5417-8f12-3e433a7e207d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 68 \\pi^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520684} {:answer/id #uuid "8600936c-7807-533f-b7ec-6363eb423607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32 \\pi^{2} \\left(- \\pi^{2} - 2\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520695} {:answer/id #uuid "afcc62a2-a04f-5e40-840e-4035cd3ad69e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi^{2} \\left(- 32 \\pi^{2} - 68\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520705} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7f42b2-a1b5-58b8-b1c4-f9b190a7088f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32 \\pi^{3} \\left(- 48 \\pi^{2} - 85\\right)}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afcc62a2-a04f-5e40-840e-4035cd3ad69e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi^{2} \\left(- 32 \\pi^{2} - 68\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520705} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3dd3542-87fa-5542-a06b-ffafba3d77a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7c78a6b5-a741-5677-9ee8-db5e516f2ee1" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=- 2 x^{2} - 2 y^{2} - 2$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=- 4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ &=(4)(-\\sin t+\\sin t+t\\cos t)i+(4)(\\cos t-\\cos t+t\\sin t)j \\\\ &=(4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+(4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{16t^2(\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t)} \\\\ &=4|t| \\\\ &=4 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t|=t$ since $t\\geq0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=- 2 x^{2} - 2 y^{2} - 2$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(-2)\\left((4 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(- 4 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2\\right)+(-2) \\\\ &=(-32)\\left(\\cos^2t+2t\\sin t\\cos t+t^2\\sin^2t+\\sin^2t-2t\\sin t\\cos t+t^2\\cos^2t\\right)+(-2) \\\\ &=(-32)(1+t^2)+(-2) \\\\ &=- 32 t^{2} - 34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C - 2 x^{2} - 2 y^{2} - 2\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}(- 32 t^{2} - 34)\\cdot (4 t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}- 128 t^{3} - 136 t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[(- 68 t^{2})+(- 32 t^{4})\\right]_{0}^{\\pi} \\\\ &=\\left((- 68 (\\pi)^{2})+(- 32 (\\pi)^{4})\\right)-\\left((- 68 (0)^{2})+(- 32 (0)^{4})\\right) \\\\ &=\\left((- 68 \\pi^{2})+(- 32 \\pi^{4})\\right)-\\left((0)+(0)\\right) \\\\ &=\\pi^{2} \\left(- 32 \\pi^{2} - 68\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520721 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0651e1c4-08b2-560b-bab1-0ee3946b48cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5245}{84} + \\frac{2720 \\sqrt{2}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520660} {:answer/id #uuid "2d9a2970-315f-5d30-bdd2-2c7a3e0457b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6 + \\frac{32 \\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520671} {:answer/id #uuid "8ee0d219-cf7d-50b1-a2df-423d51c39b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{160}{7} + \\frac{2720 \\sqrt{2}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520697} {:answer/id #uuid "a5969666-b75b-5e6c-a017-710506b5e7b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{475}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520702} {:answer/id #uuid "c083f817-fabc-53b4-9149-8f9984d36ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{127375}{189} + \\frac{306400 \\sqrt{2}}{189}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0651e1c4-08b2-560b-bab1-0ee3946b48cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5245}{84} + \\frac{2720 \\sqrt{2}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520660} :answer-field/id #uuid "763c684e-1374-5918-a1c0-00fb29101703" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "dd9ec35c-d87b-5b5e-8742-da91c43c261f" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=x + 2 y$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $$\n\\displaystyle r(t)=⟨\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3},\\,\\frac{5 t^{2}}{2} - 5 t⟩\n$$ for $t\\in [1,2].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $$\n\\displaystyle r(t)=⟨\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3},\\,\\frac{5 t^{2}}{2} - 5 t⟩,\n$$ then along the curve we have $x=\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}$ and $y=\\frac{5 t^{2}}{2} - 5 t.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{5 t^{2}}{2} - 5 t)j \\\\ &=(10 \\sqrt{t})i+(5 t - 5)j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(10 \\sqrt{t})^2+(5 t - 5)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{100t+25(t-1)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{25(t^2+2t+1)} \\\\ &=5|t+1| \\\\ &=5 t + 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t+1|=t+1$ since $t\\geq0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=x + 2 y$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(1)\\left(\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}\\right)+(2)(\\frac{5 t^{2}}{2} - 5 t) \\\\ &=\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} + 5 t^{2} - 10 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C x + 2 y\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{1}^{2}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{2}(\\frac{20 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} + 5 t^{2} - 10 t)\\cdot (5 t + 5)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{100}{3}t^{3/2}(t+1)+(50)(t^2/2-t)(t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{100 t^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{3} + \\frac{100 t^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} + 25 t^{3} - 25 t^{2} - 50 t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[\\left(\\frac{200 t^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{21}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{40 t^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{3}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{25 t^{4}}{4}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{25 t^{3}}{3}\\right)+(- 25 t^{2})\\right]_{1}^{2} \\\\ &=\\left(\\left(\\frac{200 (2)^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{21}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{40 (2)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{3}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{25 (2)^{4}}{4}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{25 (2)^{3}}{3}\\right)+(- 25 (2)^{2})\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{200 (1)^{\\frac{7}{2}}}{21}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{40 (1)^{\\frac{5}{2}}}{3}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{25 (1)^{4}}{4}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{25 (1)^{3}}{3}\\right)+(- 25 (1)^{2})\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(\\left(\\frac{1600 \\sqrt{2}}{21}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{160 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\right)+(100)+\\left(- \\frac{200}{3}\\right)+(-100)\\right)-\\left(\\left(\\frac{200}{21}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{40}{3}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{25}{4}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{25}{3}\\right)+(-25)\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{5245}{84} + \\frac{2720 \\sqrt{2}}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520724 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6809d42a-ff14-5b11-9e6c-a4c5dc0d1649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32 - 8 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520685} {:answer/id #uuid "75f20079-bf9a-5643-beb4-8aac0887b679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 - 8 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520690} {:answer/id #uuid "a3f5ade6-6985-5cb0-9970-b04d3a8c93cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 - 2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520701} {:answer/id #uuid "ba75b0a0-7b52-5b4e-be6d-4643c72bed25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 \\pi - 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520708} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd2e040-255e-5707-9f2d-893b48ce96dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64 - 32 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75f20079-bf9a-5643-beb4-8aac0887b679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 - 8 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520690} :answer-field/id #uuid "da3668a3-a325-5a48-bc73-572e9e236b2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520719}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e231449f-d0a8-51fb-ac8b-87748d209fc9" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=- y^{2}$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩$ for $t\\in [- \\frac{\\pi}{4},0].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ &=(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})i+(- 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(- 4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{16\\sin^2t+16\\cos^2t} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{16(\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t)} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{16} \\\\ &=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=- y^{2}$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(-1)(- 4 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2 \\\\ &=-16\\sin^2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C - y^{2}\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{0}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{0}(- 16 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)})\\cdot (4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{0}- 64 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=-64\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{0}\\sin^2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=-64\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{0}\\frac{1-\\cos 2t}{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=-32\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{0}1-\\cos 2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=(-32)\\left[t-\\frac{\\sin 2t}{2}\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{0} \\\\ &=\\left[(- 32 t)+(16 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)})\\right]_{- \\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{0} \\\\ &=\\left((- 32 (0))+(16 \\sin{\\left(2 (0) \\right)})\\right)-\\left((- 32 \\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right))+(16 \\sin{\\left(2 \\left(- \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\right)})\\right) \\\\ &=\\left((0)+(0)\\right)-\\left((8 \\pi)+(-16)\\right) \\\\ &=16 - 8 \\pi.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520725 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "432eecfb-20a2-5095-b3ec-3e76f9097706" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 216 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520674} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf41ec2-f489-5de9-a19a-a47e5625943d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520679} {:answer/id #uuid "6b48cc25-c525-5393-8d7c-54a84b821d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520687} {:answer/id #uuid "82514b89-cc6b-5812-8d65-61e3a30d237a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520694} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4da34d-0d0a-5dea-b628-7489bccb6cc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cf41ec2-f489-5de9-a19a-a47e5625943d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520679} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf9a4aeb-294c-5c91-aea0-4c28b6189145" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e949b5e8-0b4c-52ac-b46c-4d2d9167f454" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=- \\frac{3}{- x + y}$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨3 t,\\,3 t + 6⟩$ for $t\\in [-2,2].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨3 t,\\,3 t + 6⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=3 t$ and $y=3 t + 6.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 t + 6)j \\\\ &=(3)i+(3)j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(3)^2+(3)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{18} \\\\ &=3 \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=- \\frac{3}{- x + y}$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=\\frac{-3}{(3 t + 6)-(3 t)} \\\\ &=\\frac{-3}{6} \\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C - \\frac{3}{- x + y}\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{-2}^{2}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-2}^{2}\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\cdot (3 \\sqrt{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=(3 \\sqrt{2})\\int_{-2}^{2}- \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{-2}^{2}- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\left[t\\right]_{-2}^{2} \\\\ &=\\left[\\left(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2} t}{2}\\right)\\right]_{-2}^{2} \\\\ &=\\left(\\left(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2} (2)}{2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(\\left(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2} (-2)}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\ &=\\left((- 3 \\sqrt{2})\\right)-\\left((3 \\sqrt{2})\\right) \\\\ &=- 6 \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520728 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "145424bf-f6bb-5942-9d09-e285f663ac59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\pi^{3} \\left(5 + 6 \\pi^{2}\\right)}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520662} {:answer/id #uuid "18d47090-2dd1-5291-bb5a-e6fbf0892724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\pi + \\frac{4 \\pi^{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520664} {:answer/id #uuid "be74739c-3ea8-5708-9646-40ef9c2001d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\pi^{2} \\left(2 + \\pi^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520709} {:answer/id #uuid "bed90742-ab65-5adc-a430-b09e0b81b132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\pi^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520710} {:answer/id #uuid "ebb49685-bf7a-57be-992d-18ab3d8cc6d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\pi^{2} \\left(1 + \\pi^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebb49685-bf7a-57be-992d-18ab3d8cc6d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\pi^{2} \\left(1 + \\pi^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520726} :answer-field/id #uuid "289dda4e-7c4b-52ce-ba32-751594b39498" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ff8f8180-bdc0-5b6a-a9a7-ec6192daea60" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=x^{2} + y^{2} - 2$ along the curve $C$ parametrized by $r(t)=⟨2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=⟨2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}⟩,$ then along the curve we have $x=2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t)$ and $\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}j \\\\ &=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ &=(2)(-\\sin t+\\sin t+t\\cos t)i+(2)(\\cos t-\\cos t+t\\sin t)j \\\\ &=(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})i+(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})j \\\\ \\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{(2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{4t^2(\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t)} \\\\ &=2|t| \\\\ &=2 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t|=t$ since $t\\geq0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, if $f(x,y)=x^{2} + y^{2} - 2$, then we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(1)\\left((2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})^2\\right)+(-2) \\\\ &=(4)\\left(\\cos^2t+2t\\sin t\\cos t+t^2\\sin^2t+\\sin^2t-2t\\sin t\\cos t+t^2\\cos^2t\\right)+(-2) \\\\ &=(4)(1+t^2)+(-2) \\\\ &=4 t^{2} + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C x^{2} + y^{2} - 2\\,\\text{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}f(r(t))\\|r^{\\prime}(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}(4 t^{2} + 2)\\cdot (2 t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\pi}8 t^{3} + 4 t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[(2 t^{2})+(2 t^{4})\\right]_{0}^{\\pi} \\\\ &=\\left((2 (\\pi)^{2})+(2 (\\pi)^{4})\\right)-\\left((2 (0)^{2})+(2 (0)^{4})\\right) \\\\ &=\\left((2 \\pi^{2})+(2 \\pi^{4})\\right)-\\left((0)+(0)\\right) \\\\ &=2 \\pi^{2} \\left(1 + \\pi^{2}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "125c9fef-e1e6-59ab-a694-d2223cf1b6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "258" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536175} {:answer/id #uuid "632784b4-300a-57d6-8fbd-990ee92f3666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2052" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536196} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9d9f69-d003-56a1-8175-bb385c5221a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{513}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536211} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f82d33-be42-5959-a84f-d0438d80b642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536224} {:answer/id #uuid "e15c611b-dde5-5f8a-b2e4-d0b0be4d5705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c9d9f69-d003-56a1-8175-bb385c5221a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{513}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536211} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac87f4f-c6c9-51ac-93c4-d5e8ee44e66b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "353d7359-1a70-56e3-a4d7-6e5a53fc624b" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=9 y$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle t^{2},t\\rangle$ for $t\\in [0,2 \\sqrt{3}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=(t^{2})\\,i+(t)\\,j$, then along the curve we have $x=t^{2}$, $y=t$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j \\\\  & =(2 t)\\,i+(1)\\,j \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2 t)^2+(1)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=9 y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(9)(t) \\\\  & =9 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}(9 t)(\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=4 t^{2} + 1$, $\\text{d}u=(8 t)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{3}}9 t \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{49}\\frac{9}{8}\\cdot u^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\big|_{1}^{49} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[(49)^{3/2}-(1)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}[(343)-(1)] \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1029}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{513}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01df4532-b45d-53b7-a427-d6227daed514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536171} {:answer/id #uuid "859def66-0165-5571-8ffa-7f3709f9ec2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536206} {:answer/id #uuid "a48a6739-81cb-508a-b07a-3a3ab0634724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536214} {:answer/id #uuid "d4cecb10-b5ce-5055-ae8b-93d6718db0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536227} {:answer/id #uuid "dc68bb0d-38dd-5ebb-8d67-8a4394694daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc68bb0d-38dd-5ebb-8d67-8a4394694daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536230} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9c97da8-c43e-5d5d-9311-e6206eff1054" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3aeb7177-27b3-5c11-a4d0-3497fd32abae" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=3 y$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle t^{2},t\\rangle$ for $t\\in [0,\\sqrt{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=(t^{2})\\,i+(t)\\,j$, then along the curve we have $x=t^{2}$, $y=t$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j \\\\  & =(2 t)\\,i+(1)\\,j \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2 t)^2+(1)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=3 y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(3)(t) \\\\  & =3 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}(3 t)(\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=4 t^{2} + 1$, $\\text{d}u=(8 t)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}3 t \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot u^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\big|_{1}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(9)^{3/2}-(1)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(27)-(1)] \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{27}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536186 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0494b507-6893-5677-8d04-d371af5154b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536172} {:answer/id #uuid "1987e49f-7e77-5919-82aa-6b139e1177b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{231}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536177} {:answer/id #uuid "2285e068-d56d-5138-acec-6227d8e0efff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{341}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536179} {:answer/id #uuid "2833fcec-8de1-5841-b608-35c960c0bcd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536180} {:answer/id #uuid "eeca22e3-cbf7-5b3d-b018-b1647008ca68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2728}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2285e068-d56d-5138-acec-6227d8e0efff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{341}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536179} :answer-field/id #uuid "852e0dd8-5a52-5753-be99-a707534ca752" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3c132797-532b-531b-ac79-d0e890e2f4b0" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=11 y$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle t^{2},t\\rangle$ for $t\\in [0,\\sqrt{6}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=(t^{2})\\,i+(t)\\,j$, then along the curve we have $x=t^{2}$, $y=t$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j \\\\  & =(2 t)\\,i+(1)\\,j \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2 t)^2+(1)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=11 y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(11)(t) \\\\  & =11 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}(11 t)(\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=4 t^{2} + 1$, $\\text{d}u=(8 t)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{6}}11 t \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{25}\\frac{11}{8}\\cdot u^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{8}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\big|_{1}^{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{12}[(25)^{3/2}-(1)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{12}[(125)-(1)] \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{1375}{12}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{11}{12}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{341}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57f928b7-f3c1-52b5-b1f3-e51f2ac25685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{15 \\sqrt{14}}{26} + \\frac{45 \\sqrt{3}}{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536191} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2f52fd-d5a6-5f97-8553-e4f43e399741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 70 \\sqrt{14} + 405 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536192} {:answer/id #uuid "6a2ab4f5-0f77-542a-ae0c-3c24c174ddd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536198} {:answer/id #uuid "de7178fd-a762-590b-a176-d5866a3e8366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{35 \\sqrt{14}}{13} + \\frac{405 \\sqrt{3}}{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536231} {:answer/id #uuid "e54c1709-79ec-5e74-9903-bf87dcc8ae95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35 \\sqrt{14}}{13} + \\frac{405 \\sqrt{3}}{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de7178fd-a762-590b-a176-d5866a3e8366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{35 \\sqrt{14}}{13} + \\frac{405 \\sqrt{3}}{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536231} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f6f04f0-a3b7-5983-aafe-e6b7a4a0ae76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4598c153-f2b3-5aa3-bf7d-421ba3e4749e" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{3 y + 3 z}{x}$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle t,t^{2},\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2}\\rangle$ for $t\\in [1,\\sqrt{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=(t)\\,i+(t^{2})\\,j+\\left(\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,k$, then along the curve we have $x=t$, $y=t^{2}$, $z=\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2}$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(3 t)\\,k \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1)^2+(2 t)^2+(3 t)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13 t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{3 y + 3 z}{x}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{(3)[(t^{2})+\\left(\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2}\\right)]}{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{15}{2}\\right)t^2}{(1)t} \\\\  & =\\frac{15 t}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(\\frac{15 t}{2}\\right)(\\sqrt{13 t^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=13 t^{2} + 1$, $\\text{d}u=(26 t)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{15 t \\sqrt{13 t^{2} + 1}}{2}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{14}^{27}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{15}{52}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{52}{\\int }_{14}^{27}u^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{52}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\big|_{14}^{27} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{26}[(27)^{3/2}-(14)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{26}[(81 \\sqrt{3})-(14 \\sqrt{14})] \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{405 \\sqrt{3}}{26}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{35 \\sqrt{14}}{13}\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{35 \\sqrt{14}}{13} + \\frac{405 \\sqrt{3}}{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08930374-f1d2-5c84-b19a-2683f1af6485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 100 \\sqrt{30} + \\frac{1120 \\sqrt{14}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536173} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5c7801-aeea-5abc-8505-a02245d7ee46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{30}}{13} + \\frac{10 \\sqrt{14}}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536201} {:answer/id #uuid "af8bd43c-2eb0-5278-8be1-06e077eda466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{50 \\sqrt{30}}{13} + \\frac{560 \\sqrt{14}}{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536217} {:answer/id #uuid "e3e839ff-7be3-5f5c-93ae-9e4bc0b08ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{50 \\sqrt{30}}{13} + \\frac{560 \\sqrt{14}}{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536233} {:answer/id #uuid "e74cf37d-93ab-51d4-a5b3-0b2e116e7daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af8bd43c-2eb0-5278-8be1-06e077eda466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{50 \\sqrt{30}}{13} + \\frac{560 \\sqrt{14}}{39}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536217} :answer-field/id #uuid "d79b1b5d-3a71-51d9-b679-1016c4c4285b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536229}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4eee203b-5512-5c93-95fe-15ef6820bb5a" :question/problem "Evaluate the line integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{4 y + 4 z}{x}$ along the curve parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle 2 t,\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2},t^{2}\\rangle$ for $t\\in [\\sqrt{2},2].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s=\\int_a^b f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r(t)=(2 t)\\,i+\\left(\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,j+(t^{2})\\,k$, then along the curve we have $x=2 t$, $y=\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2}$, $z=t^{2}$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(2)\\,i+(3 t)\\,j+(2 t)\\,k \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^2+(3 t)^2+(2 t)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13 t^{2} + 4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{4 y + 4 z}{x}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{(4)[\\left(\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2}\\right)+(t^{2})]}{2 t} \\\\  & =\\frac{(10)t^2}{(2)t} \\\\  & =5 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2}f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2}(5 t)(\\sqrt{13 t^{2} + 4})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=13 t^{2} + 4$, $\\text{d}u=(26 t)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2}5 t \\sqrt{13 t^{2} + 4}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{30}^{56}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{5}{26}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{26}{\\int }_{30}^{56}u^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{26}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\big|_{30}^{56} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{39}[(56)^{3/2}-(30)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{39}[(112 \\sqrt{14})-(30 \\sqrt{30})] \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{560 \\sqrt{14}}{39}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{50 \\sqrt{30}}{13}\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{50 \\sqrt{30}}{13} + \\frac{560 \\sqrt{14}}{39}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a24a14e-7ef5-5ad1-a61b-3b0c903f1bbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{25 \\sqrt{30}}{13} + \\frac{215 \\sqrt{43}}{78}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536178} {:answer/id #uuid "32658cc0-fb41-54b1-adeb-b587a3ed9bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 50 \\sqrt{30} + \\frac{215 \\sqr